  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sharif Ahmed Shafiq Ahmed Alvi vs The State Of Maharashtra on 10 October, 2023 Author: N. J. Jamadar Bench: N. J. Jamadar 909-Aba-.2849-23.Doc Sayali Upasani In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No. 2849 Of 2023 Sharif Ahmed Shafiq Ahmed Alvi ...Applicant Vs. The State of Maharashtra ...Respondent Mr. Kushal Mor with mr. Rishab Khot , for Applicant. Mr. M. G. Patil, App for State. Mr. S. D. Ahire, Psi, Rabodi Police Station, present. Coram:- N. J. Jamadar, J. DATED:- 10th OCTOBER, 2023 PC:- 1) Heard the learned counsel for the applicant and the learned APP for the State.",
    "facts": "Subsequently, the offence punishable under Section 328 of the Penal Code seems to have been added. 3) The contraband articles - Gutka Pan Masala were found to have been stored behind the godown of the applicant's store. This is an application for pre-arrest bail in connection with CR No. 175 of 2023 registered with Rabodi Police Station, Thane for offence punishable under Section 328, 272, 273 of IPC and Section 26(2)(i), 26(2)(iv), 27(3)(e) and 30(2)(a) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. It is informed that Section 328 of IPC is invoked later on. 2. The FIR is dated 19.08.2023 and the Applicant is the sole accused. According to the FIR, the contraband articles in the form of Gutkha was found stored in a godown owned by the Applicant and therefore the FIR is filed. He submits that the 63-ABA-2849-2023.doc Applicant has been co-operating with the investigation and is also protected since 10.10.2023 under order of this Sharif Ahmed Shafiq Ahmed Alvi vs The State Of Maharashtra on 21 August, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/179718097/ 1 Court. 4. Learned APP on instructions of officer of the concerned Police Station who is present in the Court, submits that charge-sheet is already filed including for the Applicant. It is informed that case is registered as Sessions Case No. 62 of 2005 in the Sessions Court of Thane.",
    "arguments": "3. Learned Counsel for the Applicant submits that the issue as to whether Section 328 of IPC can be applied to storage of Gutkha, is pending before the Hon'ble Supreme Court.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. Learned Counsel for the Applicant submits that the issue as to whether Section 328 of IPC can be applied to storage of Gutkha, is pending before the Hon'ble Supreme Court.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
